Review teammate PR #<NUMBER> in saama-engineering/Trial-Assistant. Review only. Do NOT edit any code, do NOT commit, do NOT push, do NOT post anything to GitHub. My manager wants comments, not fixes.

STEP 0 - Isolate (no edits to my branch)
- Read the PR metadata: `gh pr view <NUMBER> --json title,body,headRefName,baseRefName,files,additions,deletions`. If it references an issue, read that too (`gh issue view <ISSUE>`) and treat its requirements as the spec.
- Create a separate worktree for the PR: `git fetch origin pull/<NUMBER>/head:review-pr-<NUMBER>` then `git worktree add ../review-pr-<NUMBER> review-pr-<NUMBER>`. Work only inside that worktree. My own branch must stay untouched.

STEP 1 - Split (no review yet)
- Group the changed files into chunks of about 300-400 changed lines each, by module or feature (e.g. tools, hooks, config, tests, frontend). Keep related files in the same chunk.
- Save the chunk list to .claude/plans/review-<NUMBER>-chunks.md with file names and line counts.
- Show me the chunks and WAIT for me to say "review chunk 1".

STEP 2 - Review one chunk per request
When I say "review chunk K":
- Read only that chunk's diff (`gh pr diff <NUMBER> -- <files>`). Open surrounding code in the worktree only when a finding needs it.
- Look for: bugs, missing or wrong permission/validation checks, behaviour that doesn't match the issue, missing or weak tests, error handling, duplicated logic, and unclear naming that breaks neighbouring conventions. Skip pure style nits.
- For each finding give: file:line, severity (Blocker / High / Nit / Question), a one-line description of the problem, and a ready-to-paste GitHub comment written politely, suggesting a fix without making it.
- Only report what you verified in the code. If you're not sure, mark it "Question" instead of stating it as a bug.
- Append findings to .claude/plans/review-<NUMBER>-findings.md.
- Then STOP and wait for the next chunk.

STEP 3 - Summary (after the last chunk)
- A short table: chunk, number of Blockers / High / Nit / Question.
- The Blockers and Highs first, then Nits and Questions.
- A list of all comments in the order I should post them on GitHub.
- Remove the worktree: `git worktree remove ../review-pr-<NUMBER>`.
